First, I open my kitchen cupboards.
What do I need for the Berlin recipe?
I look for the ingredients for the potato salad and the meatballs.
I already have onions and eggs here.
I also find a bread roll from yesterday.
That is perfect for the meatballs.
Then I write a short shopping list.
I naturally need minced meat and potatoes.
Afterwards, I note mayonnaise on the piece of paper.
And I absolutely need good mustard.
The recipe on the mobile phone is really very precise.
My shopping list is complete now.
I put my wallet into my jacket pocket.
Afterwards, I take the backpack.
A backpack is much better for heavy potatoes than a bag.
I leave the flat and lock the door.
Fortunately, the supermarket is only a few minutes away.
